<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The morning pass, at 06:00, from spec/search.yaml digest.schedule.

    cron: "0 6 * * *"      ->  StartCalendarInterval Hour 6, Minute 0
    timeout_seconds: 5400  ->  DESK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, enforced by run-digest.sh

  Why the timeout is not a launchd key: there isn't one. ExitTimeOut is the
  grace period launchd allows between SIGTERM and SIGKILL when it is already
  trying to stop the job — it does not bound how long a running job may take.
  Nothing in launchd does. So the wall-clock limit is enforced by the wrapper
  script, and this file's only job is to hand it the number.

  Why any of this matters on this machine: with Power Nap, a scheduled job
  wakes inside a short window while the lid is shut. An unsupervised job with
  no timeout that hangs — a site that accepts the connection and never answers
  is enough — stays hung indefinitely, holds the run, and KeepAlive does not
  rescue it, because from launchd's point of view the job never exited.

  The wrapper runs the whole morning pass — fetch, analyse, deliver — and the
  four values below are the ones it refuses to start without. Three of them are
  new on 23.08.2026, when the pass stopped being the digest alone: the engine,
  because `replay` against a live store returns recorded answers that look like
  real judgements, and the two ceilings on the analyst, because the only step
  that spends should say out loud how much.

  The send flag lives in the wrapper, not here. Telegram was turned on in the
  spec on 19.08.2026 and the bot credentials sit in .env, which `desk` reads at
  startup — launchd has no way to export them into this job, and hard-coding a
  token into a plist is a token in a file that is not gitignored.

  This file is not installed by anything. Copying it into ~/Library/LaunchAgents
  is a deliberate act by a human, and so is removing it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.noamarazi.jobdesk</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk/deploy/launchd/run-digest.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>DESK_HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk</string>
        <!-- The explicit wall-clock ceiling. The wrapper refuses to run without it. -->
        <key>DESK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS</key>
        <string>5400</string>

        <!-- Live judgements, not replayed cassettes. -->
        <key>DESK_ENGINE</key>
        <string>claude-code</string>

        <!-- What one morning may spend, and how many postings it may reach.
             Noam's numbers to set; these are the conservative opening values. -->
        <key>DESK_ANALYZE_BUDGET_USD</key>
        <string>2.00</string>
        <key>DESK_ANALYZE_LIMIT</key>
        <string>400</string>

        <!-- The analyst's own clock, inside the pass. It exists so an analyst
             that overruns loses its own work and not the delivery: the digest
             still goes out over the judgements already in the store. -->
        <key>DESK_ANALYZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS</key>
        <string>2700</string>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>6</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>

    <!-- Grace period after launchd asks the job to stop. Not a run-time limit. -->
    <key>ExitTimeOut</key>
    <integer>5400</integer>

    <!-- A digest is not a daemon. It runs, it prints, it exits. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk/runs/digest.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/noamarazi/Desktop/job-desk/runs/digest.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
